---
import LabShell from "../../components/lab/LabShell.astro";
import Aurora from "../../components/Aurora.astro";
import ProjectCard from "../../components/ProjectCard.astro";
import PillarBadge from "../../components/PillarBadge.astro";
import TeamCard from "../../components/TeamCard.astro";
import Card from "../../components/card/Card.astro";
import CardMedia from "../../components/card/CardMedia.astro";
import CardBody from "../../components/card/CardBody.astro";
import CardEyebrow from "../../components/card/CardEyebrow.astro";
import CardTitle from "../../components/card/CardTitle.astro";
import CardText from "../../components/card/CardText.astro";
import CardBadges from "../../components/card/CardBadges.astro";
import CardFacts from "../../components/card/CardFacts.astro";
import CardFact from "../../components/card/CardFact.astro";
import CardFooter from "../../components/card/CardFooter.astro";
import CardLink from "../../components/card/CardLink.astro";
import Badge from "../../components/Badge.astro";
---
<LabShell title="Cards" current="cards"
  intro="Cards are composed, not picked: Card is the surface, and media, badges, title, text, facts, footer and link are separate parts you arrange inside it. ProjectCard and TeamCard further down are specific cards assembled from the same parts.">

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--live">live</span>
    <h2>Composable cards</h2>
    <p><code>Card</code> is only the surface — paper, soft radius, hairline shadow, a small lift on hover.
      Everything inside is a separate part you choose and order: <code>CardMedia</code>, <code>CardBody</code>,
      <code>CardBadges</code>, <code>CardEyebrow</code>, <code>CardTitle</code>, <code>CardText</code>,
      <code>CardFacts</code> / <code>CardFact</code>, <code>CardFooter</code>, <code>CardLink</code>. A new kind
      of card is a new arrangement, not a new component. Data attributes and classes pass straight through to the
      surface, so a page's filter script can read them. Tags are <code>Badge shape="square"</code>; status
      pills are <code>Badge</code> with a status tone.</p>

    <pre class="lab-code"><code>{`<Card>
  <CardMedia src="…" />
  <CardBody>
    <CardBadges>…</CardBadges>
    <CardTitle>…</CardTitle>
    <CardEyebrow>…</CardEyebrow>
    <CardText>…</CardText>
    <CardFooter><CardLink href="…">…</CardLink></CardFooter>
  </CardBody>
</Card>`}</code></pre>

    <div class="lab-grid">
      <Card>
        <CardMedia><Aurora pillar="flow" opacity={0.7} /></CardMedia>
        <CardBody>
          <CardBadges><Badge tone="flow" size="sm" dot>Regenerative finance</Badge></CardBadges>
          <CardTitle>Media card</CardTitle>
          <CardEyebrow>Theme / category</CardEyebrow>
          <CardText>Image on top, then badges, title, eyebrow and text. This is the project card, assembled from parts.</CardText>
          <CardFooter><CardLink href="#">Read more →</CardLink></CardFooter>
        </CardBody>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardBody>
          <CardTitle>Properties card</CardTitle>
          <CardText>No image. The facts list holds any mix of values under a hairline.</CardText>
          <CardFacts>
            <CardFact label="Área">
              <Badge shape="square" size="sm">Agricultura regenerativa</Badge>
            </CardFact>
            <CardFact label="Valor a 5 años" mono>420.000 €</CardFact>
            <CardFact label="Años">4</CardFact>
            <CardFact label="Recurrencia" empty />
            <CardFact label="Viabilidad"><Badge tone="success" size="sm">Sí, viable</Badge></CardFact>
          </CardFacts>
        </CardBody>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <CardBody>
          <CardTitle>Directory card</CardTitle>
          <CardEyebrow>Murcia</CardEyebrow>
          <CardBadges>
            <Badge shape="square" size="sm">Cooperativa</Badge>
            <Badge shape="square" size="sm">Asociación</Badge>
          </CardBadges>
          <CardText>A name, a place, a few tags, a sentence — and a footer with a link and a status.</CardText>
          <CardFooter rule>
            <CardLink href="#" external>Website ↗</CardLink>
            <Badge tone="flow" size="sm">Working group</Badge>
          </CardFooter>
        </CardBody>
      </Card>
    </div>

    <p>Row layout puts the media beside the body, and the title steps up a size:</p>
    <Card layout="row">
      <CardMedia><Aurora pillar="tissue" opacity={0.7} /></CardMedia>
      <CardBody padding="lg">
        <CardBadges><Badge tone="tissue" size="sm" dot>Network coordination</Badge></CardBadges>
        <CardTitle size="lg">Row card</CardTitle>
        <CardEyebrow>Theme / category</CardEyebrow>
        <CardText>Same parts, different arrangement. On narrow screens it stacks.</CardText>
      </CardBody>
    </Card>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--live">live</span>
    <h2>Example: ProjectCard</h2>
    <p>A project summary: <code>CardMedia</code> (image, or an <code>Aurora</code> when there is none), then
      <code>CardBody</code> with <code>CardBadges</code>, <code>CardTitle</code>, <code>CardEyebrow</code>,
      <code>CardText</code> and a <code>CardFooter</code> holding a <code>CardLink</code>. The link falls back
      through <code>links.web → links.rc_page → links.karma</code> for the cohort variant, and a project with none
      of them simply renders without a footer. <code>featured</code> switches to the row layout — image left,
      content right, larger title — which is just <code>Card layout="row"</code> and
      <code>CardTitle size="lg"</code>. The smaller <code>.case-card</code> next to it is a different pattern
      (see <a class="link" href="/design-system/divider-lists/">Divider lists</a>).</p>
    <p class="lab-source">Used in: index.astro (#projects), projects.astro (full grid), NetworkSection.astro
      → projects/regenerant-catalunya (index + article, both networks), what-we-do.astro (case-card)</p>
    <div class="lab-grid">
      <ProjectCard image="/images/projects/mixite.png" title="Project heading" subtitle="Theme / category"
        body="Excerpt copy, trimmed to the first paragraph of the case-study body or a hand-curated line from landing.yaml."
        href="#">
        <Fragment slot="badges"><PillarBadge pillar="tissue" /></Fragment>
      </ProjectCard>
      <ProjectCard image={null} title="Cooperativa Exemple" subtitle="Sant Cugat · agroecology"
        body="One- or two-sentence project summary from the cohort data." href="#"
        external linkLabel="Visit site ↗" mediaPillar="flow">
        <span slot="badges" class="badge badge--success">Confirmed</span>
      </ProjectCard>
      <a class="case-card" href="#">
        <div class="case-card__media">
          <Aurora pillar="tissue" opacity={0.7} />
        </div>
        <div class="case-card__body">
          <div class="case-card__head">
            <span class="case-card__label">Case study</span>
            <span class="case-card__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </div>
          <span class="case-card__title">Case title</span>
          <p class="case-card__excerpt">Short excerpt of the linked case study.</p>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="lab-source" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);"><code>featured</code> variant — image
      left, content right, larger heading. Replaces the deleted <code>FeatureGrid</code>'s
      <code>.feat--lg</code> layout; used for the first card in <code>NetworkSection</code>'s grid (see
      Content sections). Same card, same visual language (paper/radius/shadow) — only the layout and
      heading size change. No <code>.display</code>/Averia here: that face is reserved for hero and
      page-opening moments, not card titles, however large — see Typography.</p>
    <ProjectCard featured image="/images/projects/laurel-31.png" title="Featured project heading" subtitle="Theme / category"
      body="Excerpt copy for the featured slot — same fields as the grid variant, just laid out wider with a bigger heading."
      href="#">
      <Fragment slot="badges"><PillarBadge pillar="flow" /></Fragment>
    </ProjectCard>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--live">live</span>
    <h2>Example: TeamCard</h2>
    <p>A member tile: a square <code>CardMedia</code> (the portrait, or an Averia monogram over an
      <code>Aurora</code> when there is none), then <code>CardBody</code> with <code>CardTitle</code>, a
      wide-tracked <code>CardEyebrow</code> for the role and <code>CardText</code> for the bio. The two examples
      below have no photo, so they show the monogram fallback.</p>
    <p class="lab-source">Used in: about.astro and index.astro (team roster)</p>
    <div class="lab-grid">
      <TeamCard name="Jane Doe" role="Coordination" pillar="tissue" bio="Short bio line, one or two sentences." />
      <TeamCard name="Alex Roig" role="Finance" pillar="flow" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-note">
    <strong>Done this pass:</strong> <code>ProjectCard</code> now <em>is</em> the real <code>.project-tile</code>
    pattern (index.astro and projects.astro both use it), and its second real caller, <code>NetworkSection</code>,
    was fixed to pass matching props instead of silently rendering blank cards — and restyled featured-first
    (see Content sections), using a new <code>featured</code> variant on this same component rather than
    reviving <code>FeatureGrid</code>'s separate card family. <code>ServiceCard</code> and
    <code>FeatureGrid</code> — both dead code, zero real callers — have been deleted. Divider-row patterns
    (<code>.pillar-service</code>, <code>.audiences</code>, <code>.theory</code>, <code>ProcessStrip</code>)
    moved to their own <a class="link" href="/design-system/divider-lists/">Divider lists</a> page — they aren't
    cards, and were crowding this one. <code>Tile</code> moved to <a class="link" href="/design-system/sections/">Content
    sections</a> — closer in kind to the other organisms there than to these card molecules.
    <code>TeamCard</code> was reshot from a 21/9 flat-bordered banner to a 1/1 rounded, shadowed tile
    matching <code>ProjectCard</code>'s card language — the aspect ratio now fits the square portraits
    actually on file instead of a crop chosen for the abstract placeholder.
  </div>

</LabShell>

<style>
  .lab-code {
    background: var(--surface-1); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); overflow: auto; margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-6);
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .lab-code code { font: inherit; }
  /* .case-card — from what-we-do.astro, paired there with a .pillar-service row (see Divider lists). */
  .case-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 6rem 1fr;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    transition: translate var(--t-med), box-shadow var(--t-med);
  }
  .case-card:hover { translate: 0 -2px; box-shadow: var(--shadow-md); }
  .case-card__media { position: relative; background: var(--surface-2); }
  .case-card__media img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
  .case-card__media :global(.aurora) { position: absolute; inset: 0; }
  .case-card__body { padding: var(--space-4); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-1); min-width: 0; }
  .case-card__head { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-2); }
  .case-card__label { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--text-xs); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--primary); }
  .case-card__arrow {
    width: 1.375rem; height: 1.375rem; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--umber); color: var(--paper);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    font-size: 0.7rem; flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .case-card__title { font-size: var(--text-md); }
  .case-card__excerpt { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--text-muted); line-height: var(--leading-body); margin: 0; }

  /* In the .case-card grid item specifically: size to its own content, don't stretch to match
     the taller ProjectCards it sits next to in the lab grid. */
  .lab-grid .case-card { align-self: start; }

  .lab-grid :global(.project-tile) { max-width: 22rem; }
</style>
